  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "The ratio of girls to boys in a chess club is $2:1.$ If there are $10$ girls, then how many members does the club have in total?",
  "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $2:1$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{1}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of girls, and the denominator represents the number of boys.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $10$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 5}{1\\times 5}=\\frac{10}{5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $10$ girls and $5$ boys in the club. So the total number of members is \n\n$$\n10+5=15.\n$$",
